{
 "id": "2026-11-22-m1",
 "title": "Your Wi-Fi router fires MICROWAVES 📶",
 "description": "Wi-Fi and microwave ovens both use the 2.4 GHz band. So why doesn't your router cook you? Power: an oven pumps roughly 1,000 watts into a sealed metal box, while a Wi-Fi router is capped at about 0.1 watt, spread through your house. The wave is ~12 cm long and the holes in the door screen ~1 mm, so it stays inside, flipping 2.45 billion times a second; water molecules try to turn with it, and that jostling is heat.\n\nSources: Illinois Physics Van (door screen); FCC Part 15 power limits; Physics Forums summary (oven vs router power).",
